{"kind":"report","text":"Findings. No mandatory production-code defect found in R12 candidate 94be2742e252ab1f8ef0c6bd9b442983e1982d5b, tree 8fbc0c91c6990c9583f4e70a50cef9b60edcc816. The reference inventory still describes startup counts as pending, and several seal comments retain “parser pending” despite actual adopted values. Reconcile those current-status comments when composing the union; preserve the dated historical source-preparation and diagnostic notes.\n\nReview scope. I read the 65,119-byte primary note first in full (SHA256 7458f10984db588999fbe200473bcb9ac7deff5413f5d73c45f2046b75828a2a), then the complete 89-path authored delta from dac76e3d, including bundled index/ancestry prerequisites, operator command, serving owners, configuration and test changes. Generated JS was decoded as inert JSON DATA, not evaluated. Relevant admission, registration, cleanup and publication-result contexts were also reviewed. This does not claim a fresh full read of every unchanged source file.\n\nI guarded the explicitly granted 49,288-byte summary before each read and independently matched all 89 base/candidate mode, blob, length and SHA records against immutable Git. A complete 2780-leaf comparison proves only the primary note differs from both owning-tested b7919b65 and downstream-tested 179181cb2: 2779 other descriptors are identical. Against failed-gate 386ef9cc exactly the recorded 18 paths differ, confined to fixtures/tests, W1 documentation, generated assets and note; there is no lasting production or seal/model delta. Against 49f58abf only the maintained-projection test and primary note differ. All three temporary production diagnostics are therefore exactly restored, independently of the author's restoration assertion.\n\nThe fixed index remains reachability evidence, never native authority. Unknown enforced lookups avoid raw target selection; creation lineage checks fresh indexed ancestors, exact applied births/sends and authenticated declaration closure under