h root's full guard observations, separate complete npm namespace/config-absence check, six DATA outputs/four entries/133 inputs and no signals/collector errors. Earlier 49 Native and standalone Lanes1 coverage retains its separate provenance and is not added to whole-gate counts. Reported default Page startup had 10 fixed-owner Signed admissions; hosted legacy/modern had 3/2, with actual session reads counted separately and null transport addresses. These local native paths remain below the adopted key threshold, without pretending to measure browser DOM, production addresses or throughput.\n\nMaintained Page build53185 and its separately allocated DATA comparator remain root-attributed execution. Independent current module decoding confirms HTML26184 bytes/SHA256 0167e7334fb013b0787bd559c18836789cf06d36bb2b402f1044b72ebec386f8 equals maintained src/index.html, and JS819418 bytes/SHA256 c4210f89cb676d00a2d052986916bbd3c2eb904e0c73c17043a64d56d1150525. No manual bundle edit or newly run checker build is asserted. There is no single-final-head npm gate exit 0.\n\nLanding conditions. This no-Git-artifact request attaches no Source artifact set, so this report is a local acceptance disposition, not a mergeable Gitseq approval. Preserve Main dd6e69ae's independent sprint report and the reviewed R8 behavior. The combined source has semantic overlaps: maintain fixed-index/serving admission in every sandbox service path, shared signed-stream refusal, signer-first CLI custody, real fixture registrations and all inventory controls. Compute actual changed-owner seals, rebuild the Page from the final union, compare actual data, and review its exact source and justified affected owning/final-gate results. Neither branch chain validates that new union.\n\nKeep the archive/security order and the existing R1/R2 prerequisite self-authorship qualification. Planner-owned pre-index known-root inventories, register-mode deployment and write-bearing sweep, recorded enforce deployment and exact listed verification/rollback remain required separately for all three Workers. The four SERVING_* settings, fixed index binding/migrations and mode must be recorded. Memory windows are not durable rate accounting; unknown cohorts, hosted configuration, deployment and rollout are not accepted here. No checker project/helper/parser/compiler/browser/test/build execution, install, source edit, ref change, merge, push or deployment occurred.","body":{"promise":"e8bad45b169f402bcefbd2c563be3344a45ec9e0"}}